---
// "The Secret" — MLS in three sentences for a smart, curious non-scientist.
// The emotional core: you are about to know something most people don't.
---

<section class="relative section section-loose overflow-hidden" id="the-secret">
  <!-- Faint ethereal background -->
  <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0 film-vignette edge-soak">
    <img
      src="/images/secret.jpg"
      aria-hidden="true"
      alt=""
      class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-[0.55]"
    />
    <div
      class="absolute inset-0"
      style="background:radial-gradient(110% 110% at 50% 50%, rgba(8,8,8,0.4) 0%, rgba(8,8,8,0.78) 80%)"
    >
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container-x relative z-10">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
      <p class="eyebrow justify-center mb-10 reveal">By the way</p>

      <p
        class="headline text-[clamp(2rem,5.2vw,4.5rem)] text-white leading-[1.02] reveal"
        style="transition-delay:0.05s"
      >
        So what actually is <span class="text-cyan-glow">MLS?</span>
      </p>

      <p
        class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-white/65 font-light leading-relaxed mt-12 max-w-2xl mx-auto reveal"
        style="transition-delay:0.18s"
      >
        Groups compete. Groups evolve. Once you see it you can’t unsee it.
        That’s kind of the whole show.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 reveal" style="transition-delay:0.24s">
        <a href="/start" class="btn btn-primary">Find your starting point →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
